   + the perfect battery bought at an average of 182.94 and sold at 2,532.31 USD per MWh, 2,349.37 apart, and loses 10 percent of the energy on the round trip, plus $0.11 of wear on each kWh taken out of it.
   + Your play, scored by the game's own model (lib/battery.ts, simulate) under the rules of this mode, on the day's real prices, except the emergency hour, traded at the game's prices.
   + The same battery with every price of the day known in advance, held to the game's three moves (charge at full power, sell at full power, or hold):
   + a battery free to run at part power could earn a little more.
